\name{FollowInstrumentPricing}
\alias{FollowInstrumentPricing}
\title{A pricing rule that moves a resting limit after another instrument}
\description{
The \code{follow_instrument} pricing rule of a plan: a limit moved by how far another instrument has moved since the order was sent.

The order starts at the template's own limit price, and from then on its price is that start price plus \code{delta} times the followed instrument's move, so a Nifty call bid with a delta of 0.5 rises by 20 when the index rises by 40, without reading the option's own thin book. The price stays between \code{lowest} and \code{highest}, never goes below one tick, and moves only when it would move by at least \code{step_ticks}. The template must be a limit order with a price, and the followed instrument must be another one than the order's own.
}
